<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11484"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 10:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->TAC: You may have a point about &#34;mother hatred&#34; being a main factor behind many serial killers. Edmund Kempers&#39; final murder victim was indeed his mom. He claimed &#40;paraphrasing&#41; that he &#39;killed 8 women and his mother, when I really killed 8 women INSTEAD of my mother&#39;. <BR> <BR>Son Of Sam may have harbored a deep hatred for his biological mother who had him out of wedlock &amp; gave him up to adoption. He never met her untill he was an adult, shortly before he began his serial murders. His female victims had the general appearence of what his &#39;real&#39; mom looked like as a young lady. A popular theory is that he killed young ladies which reminded him of his mom in a twisted attempt at revenge or to stop them from doing what his mom did. <BR> <BR>Ted Bundys&#39; serial murders were probably sparked by a deep loathing of his natural mother also. She  &#39;grew up&#39; with him, cruely never telling him that she was his mother. Instead she always lied to him &amp; said she was his older sister. He finally found out the truth shortly before his known killing spree. <BR> <BR>Manson also probably harbored a secret deep disgust &amp; loathing for his mommy. She was a &#34;loser&#34; alcoholic, thief &amp; prostitute. She gave up Charlie at around 10 years to a series of &#39;Boys Towns&#39; which turned out to be torturous centers of abuse &amp; rape. She often wrote  or told him that she would soon get him out- but sadly never did. <BR> <BR>The sad list may go on &amp; on. Others may know more. <BR> <BR>Victor<!--/Text--></td></tr>
