</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 10:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can go with the sykiks  as far as building a hypothesis, the police use this tactic when they are at a deadend, or have no other place to start, but things devined must also be backed up with evidence before they become fact. However is that 168 D.R. &#40;4lines from bottom, last run&#41;something she mentioned before Rader was caught?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
