<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11636"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 11:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe the BTK Strangler was motivated by hatred for his mother. The hatred stems from the oedipal complex. The Freudian psychoanalytic concept attempts to explain a son murdering his father to ensure his mother&#39;s love is directed to him. It seems during his childhood or adolescence his love for his mother was replaced by hatred. It was serious enough for him to contemplate murder and realize the fantasy later. I would suggest the female victims possessed a quality that reminded him of his mother. For the BTK Strangler, murdering the female victims symbolized murdering his mother.  <BR> <BR>Edmund Kemper is the only serial murderer, I know who resolved his oedipal trauma by murdering his mother. His hatred was so intense he decapitated her, then used her head as a dartboard and raped her headless corpse. Kemper attempted to dispose of her larynx in the garbage disposal, but it was rejected. It prompted him to state &#34;even in death she still bitched.&#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
