<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11655"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 2:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I failed to mention in my previous discussion of the oedipal complex that Big Ed Kemper murdered college students who his mother stated on numerous occasions were unobtainable. Kemper murdered college students to prove he could have &#39;relationships&#39; with refined and sophisticated young women. Kemper made an effort to undermine his mother&#39;s view. He buried the head of one victim in front of his mother&#39;s bedroom window. He was motivated by his mother&#39;s desire that &#34;people looked up to her.&#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
