<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11682"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 5:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tac,  <BR> <BR>Sally Hallett was Kemper&#39;s final victim, not his mother. She was his penultimate victim.  <BR> <BR>It should be remembered that Kemper and Kemper only provided details about his mother&#39;s death. Unless I see a police report saying so, I&#39;d consider the disposal story apocryphal. Kemper has contradicted himself a few times. The story about his mother saying &#34;Oh, I guess you want to stay up and talk all night,&#34; or words to that effect is also dubious, in my opinion. Crimelibrary provides some interesting information about Kemper. The TV special on Kemper reveals a pure sociopath; his tears during the mention of his mother&#39;s death seem forced and insincere. As sociopaths do, Kemper blamed everyone but himself for his crimes.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
