<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11750"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 6:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found a couple of instances of very abusive father&#39;s of serial killers and I am sure there are plenty more.  <BR>John Wayne Gacy had a violent alcoholic father who constantly berated him and called him a sissy, a queer and a failure. <BR>Confessed and convicted Boston strangler Albert DeSalvo&#39;s father actually sold his children as white slaves to a farmer in Maine where they remained for six months before being returned to other family members.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
