<!--Post: 11810--><!--Time: 1111204815-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11810"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 8:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tac you can ask me anything you want that is why we are hear to learn, If you look up at 3/ 17 post you will see we were working on that 2 20 11 theory It has been said that Zodiac&#39;s number is 17 I guess BTK had to have one too his is #3 and the combination of it He could have chosen the name first or the numbers first 2=b 20=t 11=k <BR>I am not sure witch came first the name or the number sequence but I am sure that like Zodiac Rader had to have a number sequence to be like the man he worshipped, The number 3 IN Raders case comes from the church the trinity, to easy I know but he had to spend his thinking time on puzzles etc, so the trinity would have been acceptable for his purpose, father, son holy ghost, just like Z&#39;s life death, rebirth. the 2 20 11 adds up to 33 and in the 3 pattern of Rader since everything is a three it becomes 333 and then of course we know that is half of 666, He could have felt that he was assisting the great Zodiac in some way. Hence the half, 333 the half he was doing for the masters. Just a theory of course and still working on it. Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11810-->
<!--Post: 11848--><!--Time: 1111279136-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11848"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 4:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E, <BR> <BR>Thanks for the kind words. Funny thing is I added up the numbers and was tinkering with 33 as well. I read a post somewhere that the Zodiac may have been fond of the number 11. The theory was based in astrology or mythology and I can not remember the theory or idea behind it.  <BR> <BR>666 being the sign of the devil has some validity in regards to the Zodiac. Many have speculated that he was somewhere along the way connected to or a disciple of a devilworship cult in the 1960&#39;s. <BR> <BR>It will be interesting to see if psychologist are able to label Rader a sociopath or if he has been listening to voices making him a paranoid schizofrenic ? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
